@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-token-here-after-login

### 1. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### 2. Readiness check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/readiness

### 3. Protected endpoint without token - should return 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assets

### 4. Login as admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}

### 5. Protected endpoint with token - should return 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Paged assets timing check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=assetTag&direction=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Invalid sort field - should return 400 if validation is enabled
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=password&direction=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Report timing check: assets by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/assets-by-status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Report timing check: assets by category
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/assets-by-category
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Duplicate asset tag check - run only if LAP-2026-001 already exists
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "LAP-2026-001",
  "name": "Duplicate Laptop",
  "category": "Laptop",
  "serialNumber": "DUPLICATE-SN-DAY17",
  "location": "Security Lab"
}
